# Background theory for the BCP 47 resource: empty.
#
# The parties declare nothing beyond the registry. The registry publishes
# no distinctness between primary subtags, so two constraints naming
# different languages are satisfiable together unless the parties adopt
# the uniqueness rule (bcp47-uniqueness.ttl).
#
# Source: https://www.iana.org/assignments/language-subtag-registry

@prefix bt:      <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/background#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47/empty> a bt:BackgroundTheory ;
    dcterms:title "No declared distinctness"@en ;
    bt:appliesTo <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47> ;
    bt:pairCount 0 .
